# video-agent-kit configuration reference.
# Copy only the entries you need into <plugin_root>/.env or <project_dir>/.env.
# Precedence: process environment > project .env > plugin .env.
# Do not put real secrets in this example file.
#
# Speech (speech_transcribe / speech_synthesize) needs NOTHING here when running
# under ZCode: the host injects identity with each tool call, so there is no key
# to configure and no endpoint to point at. Everything below is only for other
# hosts.

# --- Option 1 (recommended for non-ZCode hosts): remote HTTP MCP speech server ---
# Keeps the paid capability and its credentials on the server side.
# VE_SPEECH_MCP_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8765
# VE_SPEECH_MCP_TOKEN=

# ASR media transfer to remote MCP: auto uses shared paths for localhost and
# base64 upload for non-local servers. Set path/base64 only when deployment
# topology requires it.
# VE_SPEECH_MCP_ASR_TRANSFER=auto

# --- Option 2 (legacy escape hatch): direct HTTP speech backend ---
# For deployments that bring their own speech service. There is no built-in
# endpoint and no built-in model/resource identifier — supply your own.
#
# NOTE: the two endpoint variables are read from the PROCESS ENVIRONMENT ONLY,
# never from a .env file. A project-local .env is untrusted input: if it could
# set the endpoint, any repository could redirect a request that carries your API
# key to a host of its choosing. Export them where you spawn the server:
#   export VE_SPEECH_ASR_ENDPOINT=https://<your-speech-host>
#   export VE_SPEECH_TTS_ENDPOINT=https://<your-speech-host>
#
# The rest may live in .env:
# VE_SPEECH_ASR_RESOURCE_ID=          # required: async submit/query resource id
# VE_SPEECH_ASR_FLASH_RESOURCE_ID=    # optional: sync fallback resource id
# VE_SPEECH_ASR_API_KEY=              # single-key auth (X-Api-Key), or the pair below
# VE_SPEECH_ASR_APP_KEY=
# VE_SPEECH_ASR_ACCESS_KEY=
# VE_SPEECH_TTS_MODEL=                # required for synthesis
# VE_SPEECH_TTS_API_KEY=              # falls back to VE_SPEECH_ASR_API_KEY
# VE_SPEECH_TTS_VOICE=                # default voice / speaker id
